[38;5;231m⏺[39m I'm treating this as a bounded change: the page and the code that renders it already exist. So you'll get a short
  design here in chat, with no spec file, and I won't write any code until you approve it.

  The first question is where the filters go, and that's easier to see than to describe. I've opened three wireframes in
  a browser tab: [94m]8;id=ulch0b;http://localhost:61661/?key=b512cd52eb7547df97ddfe4ba1097dc04980498611c426440a42d58ca2ce71c6\http://localhost:61661/?key=b512cd52eb7547df97ddfe4ba1097dc04980498611c426440a42d58ca2ce71c6[39m]8;;\ (it uses
  a lot of tokens, so tell me if you'd rather stay in the terminal).

  All three sit inside the existing panel, above the table, and each shows a result count that screen readers announce:

  - [1mA. Filter bar, always visible:[0m Event, date range and search fields in one row, plus a "Clear filters" button.
    Nothing is hidden, and the row stacks on narrow screens.
  - [1mB. "Filters" button with a popover:[0m the fields open in a panel, and each applied filter shows as a removable tag.
    It's more compact, but the filters are easier to miss.
  - [1mC. Event select plus a "Show failed sign-ins" button:[0m the smallest version. It covers the case behind every support
    ticket, with no search or dates.

  I lean toward A, or C if you want the smallest diff. Have a look and tell me which you prefer. You can also click one
  in the browser. Which filters to include (dates, search) and the existing problem of the table being empty with
  JavaScript off are separate questions. I'll ask about them one at a time after this.

  One housekeeping item: the mockups are saved under [38;5;153m.hyperpowers/[39m, which isn't in [38;5;153m.gitignore[39m yet. I haven't changed
  [38;5;153m.gitignore[39m, and nothing from that folder will go into a commit.

